{"query":"Someone who couldn't afford health care under Barack Obama's Affordable Care Act gets penalized $10,000 counterevidence","results":[{"date":"Oct 20, 2020","position":1,"site_name":"www.politifact.com","snippet":"“Because our family couldn’t afford health insurance, Obama/Biden penalized us about $10,000, then took that $10,000 and used it to pay for others’ free Obamacare.","title":"A $10,000 Obamacare penalty? Doubtful. - PolitiFact","url":"https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2020/oct/28/facebook-posts/10000-obamacare-penalty-doubtful/"},{"date":"Oct 29, 2020","position":2,"site_name":"kffhealthnews.org","snippet":"The viral social media posts claim that the family “couldn’t afford health insurance” and was penalized $10,000. Health policy experts told us that while the social media post doesn’t give all the specifics needed to know if this was absolutely true, it seems unlikely a penalty would be this high.","title":"A $10,000 Obamacare Penalty? Doubtful. - KFF Health News","url":"https://kffhealthnews.org/courts/fact-check-a-10000-obamacare-penalty-doubtful/"},{"date":"Oct 22, 2020","position":3,"site_name":"leadstories.com","snippet":"Did someone who couldn't afford health care under Barack Obama's Affordable Care Act get penalized $10,000, which was then used to pay for others' free health care? And is it true that Trump \"ended that theft?\" This is a mixture of false and true.","title":"Fact Check: Trump, Congress DID End Tax Penalty For Non ...","url":"https://leadstories.com/hoax-alert/2020/10/fact-check-trump-congress-did-end-theft-of-tax-penalty-for-non-insured-but-10000-penalty-not-likely.html"},{"date":"Oct 20, 2020","position":4,"site_name":"api.politifact.com","snippet":"The viral social media posts claim that the family \"couldn’t afford health insurance\" and was penalized $10,000. Health policy experts told us that while the social media post...","title":"PolitiFact | A $10,000 Obamacare penalty? Doubtful.","url":"https://api.politifact.com/factchecks/2020/oct/28/facebook-posts/10000-obamacare-penalty-doubtful/"},{"position":5,"site_name":"www.news-medical.net","snippet":"A viral social media post claims that a family was penalized $10,000 for not being able to afford health insurance. It also claimed the penalty money was taken to pay for others'...","title":"A $10,000 Obamacare penalty? Doubtful. - News-Medical.net","url":"https://www.news-medical.net/news/20201029/A-2410000-Obamacare-penalty-Doubtful.aspx"},{"date":"Jun 4, 2024","position":6,"site_name":"www.ehealthinsurance.com","snippet":"As of 2024, tax penalties for the Affordable Care Act (also known as Obamacare) have largely been canceled. However, there are some states that still require residents to pay a fee if they don’t have health insurance. If that seems confusing, we’ll clarify it in this article.","title":"What are the tax penalties for Obamacare? | eHealth","url":"https://www.ehealthinsurance.com/resources/affordable-care-act/obamacare-tax-penalties"},{"date":"Sep 22, 2026","position":7,"site_name":"insuranceinformant.com","snippet":"Post-2019, the federal penalty for not having health insurance under the Affordable Care Act (ACA) is no longer applicable. Nevertheless, four states and D. C. maintain their own tax penalties for uninsured residents.","title":"What Is The Penalty For No Health Insurance Under Obamacare","url":"https://insuranceinformant.com/what-is-the-obamacare-penalty-for-not-having.html"}],"total_results":7,"page":0}